"DESIGN+IMPLEMENT: eliminate the possibility of forgetting a dirty flag. Analysis (2026-08-12): inverting to CLEAN flags does not remove the discipline hazard -- forgetting to CLEAR a clean flag on mutation leaves an entity marked valid while stale, the same bug mirrored -- and it fights ECS storage: iterating entities WITHOUT a component is a negative query needing a full entity scan (the cost we just deleted with the prominence system), while clean-flag rows would exist for every healthy entity (dense, permanent) versus dirty rows existing only transiently (sparse). 'Add all flags to every new entity' has the same density plus a backfill problem: each new system/flag kind requires migrating every existing entity. PROPOSED FIX: dirty flags become DERIVED FROM MUTATIONS, declared in the entity! macro schema -- e.g. a component declaration lists which flags its mutation dirties (#[component(traits in traits_components, dirties(traits_stat_block_dirty_flag))]) and every generated mutation path (insert/update/_row/_new/instantiate/delete) auto-inserts those flags. Forgetting becomes impossible because the flag follows from the mutation itself, and ALL mutations already flow through macro-generated code. Positive sparse queries stay cheap; call sites carry no discipline."